#4471 merged **412 reports** as one date bug. They hold three problems, each with its own fix.

<Callout>
One fix for #4471 would close 374 reports and leave 38 open.
</Callout>

| problem | reports | ticket |
| --- | --- | --- |
| The shared parser reads dates month first; day-first tenants get month and day flipped | 374 | [issue 1](https://github.com/DomDabrowski/mega-dev-challange-3/issues/1) |
| booking-v3 prints MM/DD/YYYY under the date field; people type what it says | 33 | [issue 2](https://github.com/DomDabrowski/mega-dev-challange-3/issues/2) |
| Bookings land exactly one day off: likely a time-zone shift, not a flip | 5 | [issue 3](https://github.com/DomDabrowski/mega-dev-challange-3/issues/3) |

## How we told them apart

Intake tags a report from the reporter's browser. That is a guess: 15 of the 33 form-hint reports were tagged `parser`. The cause depends on the tenant (its locale and booking form) and the channel, so we read it from the tenant directory.

The desk's table below counts the five one-day reports under the parser. They do not flip month and day.

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

## Lessons

- Merging by subject hides causes. Check tenant and channel before you merge.
- Intake tags are guesses; count by cause.

